WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.401
-My next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:03.636
who you can see
on the hit show "Riverdale"

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:06.272
every Wednesday night
at 8:00 p.m., on the CW.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:09.041
Here is Camila Mendes.
Oh!

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:10.543
Hey! It's so great to see you.
-Hi!

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.877
-Thank you
so much for doing this.

00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:13.679
-So good to see you, yeah.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:16.816
-Are you in Vancouver?

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.718
-I'm in Vancouver.
-Doing "Riverdale."

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:22.488
-I'm doing "Riverdale."
I just got out of quarantine

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:25.125
like two weeks ago.
-What did the cast get up to

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:27.126
when you were
in quarantine for two weeks?

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:28.861
-In quarantine?
-Yeah.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:31.864
-For the second quarantine,
like, I kind of hate it

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:36.035
when people make me feel really
[bleep] about not seeing movies.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.238
Like, if I haven't seen, like,
a really classic movie,

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.673
and people are like,
"You've never seen that?"

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.808
And they make you feel terrible.
-I know!

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:44.344
-I hate that.
I feel like it's --

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.112
-"Hey, it's fine
if you haven't seen it.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.614
We're different people,
and I have time to grow,

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:49.916
and I could watch it tomorrow."

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.984
-Yeah, there's like 500,000
movies in existence,

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:54.019
but I was like, "I've never
seen 'Lord of the Rings.'"

00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:56.156
I think I saw it
when I was like 5 years old

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:57.423
with my cousin or something.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:58.758
-Yeah.
-Don't remember it,

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.126
and every time people
talk about it,

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.360
I'm like, "Oh, I don't know,"

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.163
and they're like, "What?!"
and they freak out.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.531
So we did it in quarantine.

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:08.034
And then, we decided to watch

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:11.104
the best cinematic trilogy
of all time.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.573
-Ooh, let me think.
What is it?

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.741
"Godfather."
-"High School Musical."

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:18.144
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.478
-Yeah, that's right.
I forgot.

00:01:19.478 --> 00:01:21.080
It is "High School Musical."
I forgot.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.982
-It is "High School Musical."
-Is there three of them?

00:01:23.982 --> 00:01:26.352
-There's three of them.
And the third one, Jimmy --

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.788
the third one
you have to see it.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.423
They went all-out
for the third one.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.192
-How'd I miss the third one?

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.260
-They made it
a full cinematic experience.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.129
It went to theaters, so it
wasn't just on Disney Channel.

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:38.897
-I do remember this!
-It was in theaters.

00:01:38.897 --> 00:01:41.000
'Cause it was, like, their big
graduation, you know?

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.702
Like, saying goodbye
to the franchise

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.937
and all the characters.
And the music was next level.

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:46.239
-Yeah, not only
did I remember it,

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.441
I think I did see it
in the theaters, by the way.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:49.775
-Did you?
-Yeah, I actually did go

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:50.944
to the theater to see it

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.545
because I was actually
really psyched out.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.813
Like, me and some of the writers
were like all into it.

00:01:54.813 --> 00:01:56.482
In fact,
I totally remember this.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.184
-We were all watching it, like,
"Is this what it's gonna be like

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:01.053
when 'Riverdale's' over?"
Like, I hope they do

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:03.122
the same thing, like, we all,
like, jump into the air.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:04.990
-[ Laughing ]
Freeze frame.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.726
-[ Laughs ]
-But you're kind of --

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.061
You're kind of doing it
with this season

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.063
a little bit, though.
-Yeah, we just

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.165
had our graduation episode
last night, actually.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:16.035
-Yeah, but -- And now we get
to see the next episode,

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:19.338
what happens
to you guys in the future.

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:23.843
-We fast-forward like
seven years, or we time-jump.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.912
And now our characters
are like in their mid 20s,

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:29.081
and they all have, like,
their own separate lives.

00:02:29.081 --> 00:02:32.051
And then, Archie calls them
and kind of, like, summons them

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:35.121
back to Riverdale
for a mysterious reason.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:37.290
-You guys,
I heard that you play a game

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.691
that's kind of interesting
to me.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:41.927
-This game is actually so fun to
play, and I highly recommend it.

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:44.030
Like, when we're sitting
in our tent, really bored,

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.865
and it's, like, big days when,
like, the whole cast is there,

00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:48.734
we'll play a game called
"What Are the Odds?"

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:51.871
And, basically, you kind of,
like, pick a task.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.773
Like, I'd say,
"Jimmy, what are the odds

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:56.442
you eat an entire
watermelon right now?"

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.410
And then you have to pick
a number between 1 and 30.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.380
Like, what would you say
are your odds?

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.148
-An entire watermelon?
30.

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.183
-An entire. 30?
-Yeah.

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:06.752
-And then we would count down.

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:08.587
Like, someone would go,
"3, 2, 1,"

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:09.922
and then we'd both
have to say a number,

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:11.090
and if we say the same number,

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.926
you have to eat
that whole watermelon."

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.493
-I get it.
This is a really fun game.

00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:16.362
But it sounds dangerous
a little bit.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.164
-It is a little dangerous,
because, like,

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.432
there's some things I wouldn't
share here that we've done,

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:22.135
that we made each other do.
-Yep.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.769
-I think it's not --
-Yeah.

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:26.205
Did anyone have to eat
an entire watermelon?

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:28.474
-Oh, yeah, Drew Ray Tanner had
to eat an entire watermelon.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.875
-Oh, really?
[ Laughing ]

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.444
He looked sick to his stomach
by the end of it.

00:03:32.444 --> 00:03:34.981
We had Casey --
Casey lost one

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.116
where he had to sit
on the floor the whole day.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.918
Like, he wasn't allowed
to sit in a chair.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:39.919
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.355
It's just, like,
stupid things like that.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.891
It's not even, like,
that challenging sometimes.

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:46.425
And then, one of them,
I think --

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:47.960
I don't remember if he
ever ended up posting it,

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:50.029
but we had Charles, we said,
"What are the odds

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:53.966
you would post on your Instagram
that your lips are fake?"

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:57.437
Like, make a video confessing
that you have fake lips.

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:59.438
And I think he did it
and then deleted it,

00:03:59.438 --> 00:04:00.506
'cause we were like, "Oh, wait.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:01.874
People might actually
believe you."

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:04.110
I don't remember.
-Camila, I always love

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.177
having you on the show,

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:07.614
but I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:10.983
Here's Camila Mendes in next
week's episode of "Riverdale."

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:12.218
Take a look at this.

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.954
-It's 2021, Chad.
Haven't you heard?

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:17.456
Women can have it all now.

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:19.358
-I just...

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:21.661
I don't want you
to be unduly stressed.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:24.063
-I'm not stressed.

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:26.799
Actually, I miss being on
the trading floor with you.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.467
I miss all that adrenaline.

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:32.472
The highs of a filthy huge sale,
talking smack with the guys.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:34.040
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:38.010
They called me
the She-Wolf of Wall Street.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.812
Camila Mendes.
"Riverdale" airs

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:42.081
Wednesday nights
at 8:00 p.m., on the CW.

